WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.812
This is the first runnable PostgreSQL example in the
module Do

00:00:05.826 --> 00:00:09.670
not try to memorize it Read it from top to bottom
and

00:00:09.697 --> 00:00:15.412
identify the purpose of each statement The first
statement removes an earlier

00:00:15.439 --> 00:00:18.715
practice table if it exists so the example is safe
to run

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:24.375
again CREATE TABLE defines a small table INSERT INTO
adds

00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:29.939
one row SELECT reads the rows back Before

00:00:29.965 --> 00:00:34.560
you click Run predict the final output You should
expect one row

00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:39.648
with the patient ID and patient name that were
inserted Run the

00:00:39.674 --> 00:00:44.071
code directly in the browser and inspect the result
Then if you

00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:48.084
want copy it into pgAdmin's Query Tool and run the
same three-step

00:00:48.098 --> 00:00:53.965
sequence there The goal is simply to connect CREATE
INSERT and SELECT

00:00:53.978 --> 00:00:55.149
with what each one does
